From: jiashuaiquan <jiashuaiquan@asterfusion.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:32:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: fix sta UAF after peer unmap

Late TX completion can still look up a link peer after HTT unmap
has already freed it, then pass the stale peer->sta into
ieee80211_tx_status_ext(). That walks a torn-down sta_info and
crashes in get_link_sta / vif.type.

Clear the RCU-visible link_peers entry and peer->sta first so new
and in-flight readers stop using the station, then defer the free
with call_rcu until existing RCU read-side critical sections end.

Tested on AP7330 (ipq53xx), verified STA disconnect/reconnect no longer
hits the unmap UAF.

Fixes: WIFI-15395
Signed-off-by: jiashuaiquan <jiashuaiquan@asterfusion.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_peer.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_peer.h
@@ -146,6 +146,7 @@ struct ath12k_dp_link_peer {
 	u32 atf_actual_ul_duration;
 
 	bool is_assigned;
+	struct rcu_head rcu;
 };
 
 struct ath12k_dp_peer {
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_peer.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_peer.c
@@ -172,6 +172,17 @@ bool ath12k_dp_link_peer_exist_by_vdev_id(struct ath12k_dp *dp, int vdev_id)
 	return false;
 }
 
+static void ath12k_link_peer_free_rcu(struct rcu_head *head)
+{
+	struct ath12k_dp_link_peer *peer = container_of(head, struct ath12k_dp_link_peer,
+							rcu);
+
+	kfree(peer->peer_stats.rx_stats);
+	kfree(peer->peer_stats.tx_stats);
+	kfree(peer->peer_stats.qos_stats);
+	kfree(peer);
+}
+
 void ath12k_link_peer_free(struct ath12k_dp_link_peer *peer)
 {
 	if (!peer)
@@ -203,7 +214,12 @@ void ath12k_peer_unmap_event(struct ath12k_base *ab, u16 peer_id)
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_PEER, "htt peer unmap vdev %d peer %pM id %d\n",
 		   peer->vdev_id, peer->addr, peer_id);
 
-	ath12k_link_peer_free(peer);
+	if (peer->dp_peer && peer->link_id < ATH12K_NUM_MAX_LINKS)
+		rcu_assign_pointer(peer->dp_peer->link_peers[peer->link_id], NULL);
+	WRITE_ONCE(peer->sta, NULL);
+
+	list_del(&peer->list);
+	call_rcu(&peer->rcu, ath12k_link_peer_free_rcu);
 	wake_up(&ab->peer_mapping_wq);
 
 exit:
